Mail fraud involves using the United States Postal Service to perpetrate a scheme to defraud. It is a federal felony and can be charged as a standalone crime or in connection with another crime such as extortion or wire fraud.
The key elements of mail fraud are:
a false or fraudulent representation;
made with the intent to defraud;
to a person;
by mail

A few years ago I was working on a project that involved a lot of sensitive information and had to write some scripts and utilities to protect it. This was the result.
#!/bin/bash echo "You have been denied access to this website. Please contact the owner for more information."
#!/bin/bash echo "You have been denied access to this website."
The first script denies access to the website by echoing a generic deny message. The second script denies access and provides more details.
This script is a simple example but you could use it as a base for your own needs.

